message.content:
Build career page enhancements (Batch 1) for Rankora at `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Rankora`: **SEO + JSON-LD**, **Job Detail Page**, **View/Apply Tracking**.

Read CLAUDE.md first. Then read these files:
- `src/pages/CareerPage.tsx` — current public career page
- `src/pages/CareerSettings.tsx` — admin career settings
- `src/components/career/JobListingCard.tsx` — job card component
- `src/components/SeoHead.tsx` — existing SEO component
- `src/pages/Apply.tsx` — apply page pattern
- `supabase/migrations/20260407300000_add_career_page.sql` — DB schema

---

## Feature A: SEO Meta Tags + JSON-LD Structured Data

### Add to CareerPage.tsx
Add dynamic `<head>` meta tags using `useEffect` + `document.head`:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!config) return;
  document.title = `Careers at ${config.company_name} | Rankora`;

  // Set meta tags
  const setMeta = (name: string, content: string) => {
    let el = document.querySelector(`meta[property="${name}"]`) || document.querySelector(`meta[name="${name}"]`);
    if (!el) { el = document.createElement("meta"); el.setAttribute(name.startsWith("og:") ? "property" : "name", name); document.head.appendChild(el); }
    el.setAttribute("content", content);
  };

  setMeta("description", config.tagline || `View open positions at ${config.company_name}`);
  setMeta("og:title", `Careers at ${config.company_name}`);
  setMeta("og:description", config.tagline || `View open positions at ${config.company_name}`);
  setMeta("og:type", "website");
  setMeta("og:url", window.location.href);
  if (config.logo_url) setMeta("og:image", config.logo_url);

  return () => { document.title = "Rankora"; };
}, [config]);
```

### Add JSON-LD for each job listing
Add a `<script type="application/ld+json">` in the page for JobPosting schema:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!jobs.length || !config) return;
  const jsonLd = {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "ItemList",
    itemListElement: jobs.map((job, i) => ({
      "@type": "ListItem",
      position: i + 1,
      item: {
        "@type": "JobPosting",
        title: job.title,
        description: job.job_description?.slice(0, 500) || job.title,
        datePosted: job.created_at,
        employmentType: job.employment_type?.toUpperCase().replace("-", "_") || "FULL_TIME",
        jobLocation: job.location ? { "@type": "Place", address: { "@type": "PostalAddress", addressLocality: job.location } } : undefined,
        hiringOrganization: { "@type": "Organization", name: config.company_name, logo: config.logo_url || undefined },
        applicantLocationRequirements: job.location ? { "@type": "Country", name: job.location } : undefined,
        directApply: true,
      }
    }))
  };

  let script = document.getElementById("career-jsonld");
  if (!script) { script = document.createElement("script"); script.id = "career-jsonld"; script.setAttribute("type", "application/ld+json"); document.head.appendChild(script); }
  script.textContent = JSON.stringify(jsonLd);

  return () => { document.getElementById("career-jsonld")?.remove(); };
}, [jobs, config]);
```

---

## Feature B: Job Detail Page

### New page: `src/pages/CareerJobDetail.tsx`

Route: `/careers/:slug/jobs/:jobId`

This is a PUBLIC page (no auth) that shows the full job description + metadata + apply button.

**Layout:**
- Same header/footer as CareerPage (branded, responsive)
- Breadcrumb: Company Name > Jobs > Job Title
- Left column (2/3): Full job description, requirements, responsibilities
- Right column (1/3): Job metadata card (location, department, type, salary, posted date) + Apply button
- "Apply Now" button links to `/apply/:jobId`
- Back to all jobs link
- Social sharing buttons (same as JobListingCard)
- Related jobs section at bottom (other published jobs from same company)
- JSON-LD for individual JobPosting

**Fetch job data:**
```tsx
const { data: job } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ["career-job", slug, jobId],
  queryFn: async () => {
    const { data } = await (supabase as any)
      .from("jobs")
      .select("id, title, job_description, location, department, employment_type, salary_range, created_at, is_published")
      .eq("id", jobId)
      .eq("is_published", true)
      .single();
    return data;
  },
});
```

Also fetch the career config for branding (same query as CareerPage).

**Job description rendering:**
The `job_description` field is plaintext. Render it with proper line breaks:
```tsx
<div className="prose prose-sm max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
  {job.job_description.split("\n").map((line, i) => (
    line.trim() ? <p key={i}>{line}</p> : <br key={i} />
  ))}
</div>
```

### Update CareerPage.tsx
- Change "Apply Now" button on each JobListingCard to link to `/careers/${slug}/jobs/${job.id}` instead of directly to `/apply/${job.id}`
- Add a "View Details" link alongside Apply on each card

### Update App.tsx
Add route: `<Route path="/careers/:slug/jobs/:jobId" element={<CareerJobDetail />} />` — public, outside MaintenanceGate.

---

## Feature C: View/Apply Tracking

### DB Migration: `supabase/migrations/20260408600000_add_career_analytics.sql`

```sql
-- Job view tracking
CREATE TABLE public.job_views (
  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  job_id uuid NOT NULL REFERENCES public.jobs(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  viewer_ip text,
  referrer text,
  created_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_job_views_job ON public.job_views(job_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_job_views_created ON public.job_views(job_id, created_at);

ALTER TABLE public.job_views ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Anyone can insert views (public pages)
CREATE POLICY "Public can track views"
  ON public.job_views FOR INSERT TO anon, authenticated
  WITH CHECK (true);

-- Only job owner/team can read view stats
CREATE POLICY "Job team can view analytics"
  ON public.job_views FOR SELECT TO authenticated
  USING (
    EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM public.jobs j
      LEFT JOIN public.team_members tm ON tm.team_id = j.team_id AND tm.user_id = auth.uid()
      WHERE j.id = job_views.job_id
      AND (j.user_id = auth.uid() OR tm.user_id IS NOT NULL)
    )
  );

-- Add view_count and apply_count as materialized fields on jobs for performance
ALTER TABLE public.jobs ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS view_count integer DEFAULT 0;
ALTER TABLE public.jobs ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS apply_count integer DEFAULT 0;

-- Function to increment view count
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.increment_job_view(p_job_id uuid, p_ip text DEFAULT NULL, p_referrer text DEFAULT NULL)
RETURNS void
LANGUAGE plpgsql
SECURITY DEFINER
SET search_path = public
AS $$
BEGIN
  INSERT INTO public.job_views (job_id, viewer_ip, referrer) VALUES (p_job_id, p_ip, p_referrer);
  UPDATE public.jobs SET view_count = view_count + 1 WHERE id = p_job_id;
EXCEPTION WHEN OTHERS THEN NULL;
END;
$$;

GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION public.increment_job_view(uuid, text, text) TO anon;
GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION public.increment_job_view(uuid, text, text) TO authenticated;

-- Trigger to increment apply_count when application is created
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.increment_apply_count()
RETURNS trigger
LANGUAGE plpgsql
SECURITY DEFINER
SET search_path = public
AS $$
BEGIN
  UPDATE public.jobs SET apply_count = apply_count + 1 WHERE id = NEW.job_id;
  RETURN NEW;
EXCEPTION WHEN OTHERS THEN
  RETURN NEW;
END;
$$;

CREATE TRIGGER trg_increment_apply_count
  AFTER INSERT ON public.applications
  FOR EACH ROW
  EXECUTE FUNCTION public.increment_apply_count();
```

### Track views on CareerJobDetail.tsx
On mount, call the RPC to log a view:
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!jobId) return;
  (supabase as any).rpc("increment_job_view", { p_job_id: jobId, p_referrer: document.referrer || null }).catch(() => {});
}, [jobId]);
```

### Show view/apply counts in CareerSettings.tsx
In the published jobs list, show small badges: "X views · Y applications" per job. Fetch from jobs table (view_count, apply_count fields).

### Show in JobDetailView too
In the job header area of JobDetailView, show view_count and apply_count as small stat badges next to the title.

---

## Constraints
- NEVER edit `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts`
- `(supabase as any)` for new tables/columns
- `@/` imports, shadcn-ui only, Sonner toasts
- Public pages: no auth required
- Run `npm run build` at end — zero TypeScript errors

